.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt LOG4U 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm log4u
.Nd lightweight logging library for POSIX shell scripts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&. ./log4u

log4u_init [configuration-file]

log4u_debug [message ...]
log4u_info  [message ...]
log4u_warn  [message ...]
log4u_error [message ...]
log4u_fail  [message ...]
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a sourceable logging library for POSIX-compatible shell scripts.
It provides level filtering, separate console and file outputs, optional
console colors, and a small runtime control API.
.Pp
Configuration is optional.
Immediately after the library is sourced, console logging is enabled at
.Sy INFO
level, colors are disabled, and file logging is disabled.
.Pp
The levels, from most to least verbose, are:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Sy DEBUG
.It
.Sy INFO
.It
.Sy WARN
.It
.Sy ERROR
.It
.Sy FAIL
.El
.Pp
A threshold includes its named level and every more severe level.
For example,
.Sy WARN
allows
.Sy WARN ,
.Sy ERROR ,
and
.Sy FAIL .
.Sh QUICK START
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/bin/sh

\&. ./log4u

log4u_info "service started"
log4u_warn "retrying connection"

if ! result=$(perform_request); then
        log4u_error "request failed"
        exit 1
fi

log4u_debug "response:" "$result"
.Ed
.Pp
All message arguments are joined with a single space.
Quote an argument when whitespace inside that argument must be preserved.
.Sh FUNCTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic log4u_debug Op Ar message ...
Writes a
.Sy DEBUG
message when an enabled output accepts that level.
.It Ic log4u_info Op Ar message ...
Writes an
.Sy INFO
message.
.It Ic log4u_warn Op Ar message ...
Writes a
.Sy WARN
message.
Console output is sent to standard error.
.It Ic log4u_error Op Ar message ...
Writes an
.Sy ERROR
message.
Console output is sent to standard error.
.It Ic log4u_fail Op Ar message ...
Writes a
.Sy FAIL
message.
Console output is sent to standard error.
.It Ic log4u_init Ar configuration-file
Validates and applies a configuration file.
The active configuration is unchanged if validation fails.
This function may be called repeatedly.
.It Ic log4u_reset
Restores the default configuration.
.It Ic log4u_status
Prints the active color, console, file, mode, and threshold settings.
.It Ic log4u_set_console_level Ar level
Changes the console threshold.
.It Ic log4u_get_console_level
Prints the console threshold.
.It Ic log4u_set_file_level Ar level
Changes the file threshold.
The setting is retained even when file output is currently disabled.
.It Ic log4u_get_file_level
Prints the file threshold.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Configuration files contain one property per line.
Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is
.Ql #
are ignored.
Keys are case-sensitive, surrounding whitespace is allowed, and the last
occurrence of a duplicate property wins.
Unknown properties and invalid values cause initialization to fail.
.Pp
The supported properties are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy LOG4U.CONSOLE
Enables console output.
.It Sy LOG4U.CONSOLE.LEVEL= Ns Ar level
Sets the console threshold.
The default is
.Sy INFO .
.It Sy LOG4U.LOGCOLORS
Enables ANSI colors for console output.
File output never contains color escapes.
.It Sy LOG4U.LOGFILE= Ns Ar filename Ns Op ,a|d
Enables file output.
Mode
.Cm a
appends and is the default.
Mode
.Cm d
deletes an existing file during initialization; subsequent messages create
and append to a new file.
.It Sy LOG4U.LOGFILE.LEVEL= Ns Ar level
Sets the file threshold.
The default is
.Sy INFO .
.El
.Ss Complete configuration example
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Console: warnings and above, with colors
LOG4U.CONSOLE
LOG4U.CONSOLE.LEVEL=WARN
LOG4U.LOGCOLORS

# File: every message, replacing the previous run
LOG4U.LOGFILE=application.log,d
LOG4U.LOGFILE.LEVEL=DEBUG
.Ed
.Pp
Load the configuration and handle errors explicitly:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if ! log4u_init ./log4u.conf; then
        printf '%s\en' "cannot initialize logging" >&2
        exit 1
fi
.Ed
.Sh OUTPUT FORMAT
Each entry contains a local ISO 8601 timestamp with UTC offset, process ID,
level, script name, and message:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
2026-07-30T14:30:00+0200 [12345] INFO ./worker.sh: service started
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy DEBUG
and
.Sy INFO
console messages use standard output.
.Sy WARN ,
.Sy ERROR ,
and
.Sy FAIL
console messages use standard error.
All file messages use the configured logfile.
.Pp
Multiline messages are preserved verbatim.
Only the first physical line receives the metadata prefix; later physical
lines are continuation lines.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Set
.Va log4u_trace
to a nonempty value to enable shell execution tracing inside the library:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
log4u_trace=1
log4u_init ./log4u.conf
log4u_trace=
.Ed
.Pp
Tracing may expose message or configuration data and should only be enabled
during development.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ./log4u
The sourceable library.
.It Pa ./log4u.conf
Example configuration.
.It Pa ./test
The bats-core behavioral test suite.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Use different thresholds
.Bd -literal -offset indent
log4u_set_console_level ERROR
log4u_set_file_level DEBUG

log4u_debug "written only to the logfile"
log4u_error "written to both enabled outputs"
.Ed
.Ss Inspect and reset state
.Bd -literal -offset indent
log4u_status
printf 'console threshold: %s\en' "$(log4u_get_console_level)"

log4u_reset
.Ed
.Ss Log multiple values safely
.Bd -literal -offset indent
user="Ada Lovelace"
attempt=3
log4u_info "login attempt" "$attempt" "for user" "$user"
.Ed
.Ss Log a multiline message
.Bd -literal -offset indent
details='first line
second line'
log4u_error "$details"
.Ed
.Ss Check for an output failure
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if ! log4u_info "checkpoint reached"; then
        printf '%s\en' "log output failed" >&2
fi
.Ed
.Ss Log before initialization
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&. ./log4u
log4u_info "using default console configuration"
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Functions report success and failure with the following return statuses:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The operation succeeded.
A filtered message also returns zero.
.It 1
Configuration loading failed, timestamp creation failed, or an enabled output
could not be written.
.It 2
An API function received an invalid number of arguments or an invalid runtime
level.
.El
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
.Nm
targets POSIX
.Xr sh 1 .
It is also usable from Bash and KornShell.
.Pp
The original camel-case API remains available through compatibility aliases:
.Bl -column -offset indent "Current function" "Compatibility alias"
.It Sy Current function Ta Sy Compatibility alias
.It log4u_reset Ta logReset
.It log4u_status Ta logStatus
.It log4u_set_console_level Ta logSetLevel
.It log4u_get_console_level Ta logGetLevel
.It log4u_init Ta logInit
.It log4u_debug Ta logDebug
.It log4u_info Ta logInfo
.It log4u_warn Ta logWarn
.It log4u_error Ta logErr
.It log4u_fail Ta logFail
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr printf 1 ,
.Xr sh 1
